  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Ukraine crisis - cash voucher assistance and restoring family links</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">15,000 vulnerable family members of missing people enrolled in the URCS Tracing program people supported with MPCA to cover their basic needs.
3,000 families with missing people supported with a cash top-up to cover missing status related expenditure.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disappearance of a breadwinner causes economic instability for families and dependants.
Legal procedures to establish missing person status are often lengthy and costly.
Families are not eligible for state benefits and support unless they have missing status</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide cash assistance to vulnerable families of missing persons.
Offer financial support packages to support basic needs and missing status related expenses.
Alleviate economic strain and facilitate navigation of legal complexities.
Mainstream the use of cash assistance as part of the complementary/integrated support provided by URCS to vulnerable groups to maximize impact and outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will cover all regions of Ukraine, acknowledging that missing individuals may originate from different parts of the country; considering also that most acute caseloads will originate from areas intensely affected by active conflict, including those currently under occupation or previously occupied, where families face heightened uncertainties and challenges in locating their missing ones</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To mitigate the economic challenges faced by vulnerable families of missing persons enrolled in URCS Tracing program, by the provision of targeted and complementary cash assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
